My third ascention, and my second one in a month. Apparently, I've got
the hang of this game finally!

I've been trying and trying to get a Rogue started for a few weeks, and
I just couldn't get a good game going. This game, believe it or not, I
found a Blessed Magic Lamp on DL1 (!), an uncursed one in Gnome1, a
cursed one in the Gnome City, and another uncursed one around d6. So,
my early game was pretty much assured. I made sure they were all
blessed via the altar on DL2, and got 3 wishes out of them (Gray scale,
Speed boots, and a Magic Marker). I cleaned out the mines and found a
ring of conflict. A few sacrifices on DL2 and I get Stormbringer (like
only 4 offerings!), so I throw on the Conflict ring and wear it the
entire game. I end up dual-wielding Stormbringer and an Elven
Broadsword.

Sokoban was on 7, I cleared that out and got the Bag of Holding, which
was sorely needed. Blessed it and headed downwards, finding an altar on
9 and an unaligned temple on 10. I paid the priest there for some
protection and got about 4 points from him. I set up a headquarters on
level 9 and started carting everything I found to my treasure chest
there. I was trying to go Polyless this game, but I figured it was a
good idea to prepare for an eventual polypile if needed. Good thing
too, as it didn't turn out.

I found a corpse of one of my previous chars, a dual Silver Spear
wielding Barbarian, on level 11. This guy had quite a lot of stuff, and
my headquarters was just 2 levels away, so I intended to take
everything there, BCU it, and do a blessed remove curse. So, I'm
picking things up off the corpse and putting them into my bag, very
carefully avoiding the wands that might be Cancellation.

Then, the first mishap of the game.

I was putting a bunch of stuff in my bag of holding (which I always
assign to 'b'), when I got distracted with something outside the game
for a moment. Coming back, I thought I was picking stuff up off the
ground, and just told it to pick up everything. Oops! Turns out I was
putting stuff into my Bag of Holding. BOOM! No clue what I actually
lost in the explosion, but I was left with a cursed bag of holding
(from the corpse) and no holy water. Well, best to make the most of it,
so I started taking stuff out of the cursed bag and filling my
inventory (since it was too heavy to carry). Now, I'm firmly in the
habit of doing "abi' and 'abo' to put things in and out of my bag of
holding -- I don't even really think about it anymore. So, I picked up
a load of stuff and instinctively hit 'abi' to put stuff in. Up pops my
inventory screen! Oh yeah, I have no bag. What's b?

A freaking cursed blindfold. Very funny, RNG, very funny.

So, I panicked and logged out for the night.

The next day, I got back in and looked at the icons for the potions,
found the ones that looked like water, and started dipping the
blindfold. Luckily, there was some holy water on the barbarian's
corpse, and the blindfold slipped off. Thank you, Windows tileset! Was
that cheating?

Anyway, I get everything back to the HQ on 9, BCU it, Blessed Remove
Curse it, and find a bunch of cool potions, scrolls and wands. I quaff
2 Gain Levels (from the corpse, he was saving em) to get up to level
14, and head to the quest on level 12. Walk in, kill one Nymph, and
there's a Master Lich standing there. Ha! "I'll be back" Fleshpile the
Third says.

Continuing down, I discover another altar on level 17, so I drag my
treasure chest from HQ down to level 17 and set up what would turn out
to be my permanent HQ. I do a bunch of sacrificing, using my bag of
tricks, wands of create monster, etc, and come up with Sunsword,
Trollsbane, Firebrand, Frostbrand, and am declared the Glory of
Atrioch.

Heading down again, Rogue Level is on 18, an aligned temple on 19, an
altar on 21, and another aligned temple on 26. Apparently it's a
religious holiday in the Dungeons of Doom! I pay to get my unarmored AC
down to 0.

Medusa's Isle is on 27, and I still don't have a Ring of Levitation OR
Boots of Jumping. *sigh* Well, there goes the polyless conduct! I head
back to HQ and go polymorph crazy. Magic Marker a stack of Blessed
Identifies and ID pretty much everything in the game, I get the
Levitate ring, head down to Medusa's Isle and to the Castle.

The wand in the Castle has 3 charges. I already had a blessed charging
scroll, so I got 2 Blessed Scrolls of Genocide (for Liches and Mind
Flayers), a Helm of Telepathy, another Magic Marker, an Amulet of
Reflection, a Cloak of Magic Resistance (I wanted BLACK dragon armor
eventually, since I'm a chaotic Rogue!), and 2 Potions of Gain Energy
(for alchemy later, since I hadn't ID'd that potion yet, or even gotten
one).

Going very well at this point! I head back to HQ to unload, then to 12
to the quest. Now that I've taken out the Liches, it's safe to enter.
OMG the Rogue quest is annoying. I fell through a pit and ended up in
one of the "no way out of this room" parts of the quest, and almost did
a #quit because I couldn't find a way out. After consulting this forum
about level teleport, I discover how useful Tripe Rations really are. I
eat the dog food, puke, and read a teleport scroll in confusion. After
wandering around the quest for a while, I shrugged and decided to just
come back later. I didn't have any Teleport scrolls left, and really
didn't wanna get trapped.

So, back to the Dungeon! I re-equip again at HQ and do some alchemy. I
have saved ALL my healing potions, so I come out with like 30 blessed
full healing potions, and I have a drink-a-thon, getting me to around
400 hit points.

Time to head to Gehennom. They sure give you an assload of stuff in the
Valley of the Dead! I got a bunch of scrolls, blanked 'em, penned some
Magic Mapping, and got to work doing some cartography. Believe it or
not, Gehennom was fairly boring! /sarcasm

I find a Black Dragon finally, kill & eat it, get hard (no, not that
way), and grab his scales. Back to HQ for a sec, I pen a few Enchant
Armors and replace my Gray scale with Black Dragon Scale Mail. Now, I'm
an evil rogue :).

So I ran out of blank scrolls at Orcus' Lair, and wandered around in
the dark all the way down to the end at 49. Found the Vibrating Square
and marked it, and headed back to find Vlad's. Looking and looking and
looking for HOURS, and couldn't find it. Turns out, it was back in
Orcus' Lair the whole time. Oops!

Went in and took him out, found the amulet of Life Saving, and got the
Candelabra. Back down to the Wizard, there's a zillion gremlins hanging
out in his little watery tower. Good thing this Ring of Conflict has
served me so well this game, they all kill eachother without any
hassle. I kill the wizard and get the Necronomicon, and head down to
49.

Dig, dig, dig, down to 49 I go. Strange vibration! I attach the
candles! I check my inventory for the book and the b... the b... uhh...
OH MY GOD. I never finished the quest! I don't have the bell! But I've
already killed the wizard, and now he's gonna pester me all day. Yikes
what a dork I am. Better turn around!

Head up, up, up to level 12, into the quest. I have a whole bunch of
teleport scrolls now, so I dig in, zap a Polymorph wand at the Assassin
and turn him into something pathetic, and kill him in one hit. Take
that, Assassin! Dogfood-teleport out of the quest and walk down, down,
down to 49. Oddly, the wizard only harassed me twice during that whole
fiasco. Thanks, Rodney!

I light the candles! I ring the bell! I read the book! Poof! I go down,
walk around the temple ringing the bell, find the door and kill the
priest (easily). Grab the amulet & name it, and head up, up, up! The
mysterious force was as merciful as I've ever seen it, only hit like 6
times, and 4 of those it put me on the same level. Thanks, RNG!

Float over the isle, over the moat, and up to 17 to dump off everything
at HQ. I grab all my teleport wands, all my gems, all my gold, and all
my artifacts, and I'm burdened. I guess 90,000 gold is too much to
carry, so I leave it. Kos doesn't need my money anyway ;).

Up to 1, I do a final inventory check and proceed to the Elemental
Planes.

Earth is no problem, I have like 10 digging wands so I just zap around
till I find the portal.

Air is somewhat challenging, as I just can't find that portal. I use
one of my two charges on my crystal ball and find it.

Fire is irritating. Sooooooo slowwwww.... Every time I move, 10
creatures have to resist fire traps and fire breath etc since I have
Conflict on. I try the crystal ball and it blows up. Drat. About an
HOUR later I find the portal. Gah!

Water is a little time-consuming, but no biggie. I find the portal
and...

The Astral Plane! I slay the Conflict angel in a few hits, and a cobra
spits in my eye, activating my telepathy to see the riders. Death is
left, Famine is middle, Pestilence is right. My previous 2 ascensions
have been in the middle, so I'm going there first. I fight my way
straight up, zap Famine with a Wand of Death, and walk in. Whaddaya
know, it's middle again ;). Remove Stormbringer and Conflict, #chat at
the priest and he gives me some beer money. Thanks, father!

Ahh, ascension. So wonderful.

